WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Begin with a known result
The default due-date report starts with invented work orders. No CSV has been imported.
Check the starting point before changing the dataset.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Preview before writing
Load the included synthetic sample and inspect every row. Preview leaves the report at nine orders.
All rows must pass. Apply is a separate, explicit action.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Commit the orders and receipt together
Apply adds three orders and two completion events. Their receipt commits in the same SQLite transaction.
If receipt storage fails, the whole import rolls back.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Inspect the stored explanation
View the saved receipt and download its exact JSON bytes. Raw CSV contents and filenames are not stored.
The displayed ID and time are fixed fictional capture fixtures.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Restart the app; reopen the receipt
The original app process stops. A new process opens the same database and downloads the identical receipt.
The browser download bytes match the first download exactly.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Restore into a fresh directory
Stop the app, back up, verify and restore with the CLI. Reopen the new copy and download the receipt again.
This is local history, not a signed audit log or a power-loss guarantee.
